          "quote": "(node (ref \"U1\") (pin \"3\") (pinfunction \"VI\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "an ATtiny-driven fan controller"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The SDA line is held at the input-supply voltage and cannot function as a normal bidirectional data line. Pulling it low may also cause excessive current or damage, depending on the supply and connected devices.",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "category": "extra_component",
      "components": ["U2", "U3"],
      "pins": ["U2.1", "U3.1", "U2.2", "U3.2", "U2.3", "U3.3", "U2.4", "U3.4", "U2.5", "U3.5", "U2.6", "U3.6", "U2.7", "U3.7", "U2.8", "U3.8"],
      "nets": ["+5V", "GND", "POT", "PWM", "RST", "SCK", "SDA", "TACH"],
      "observed": "Both U2 (ATtiny45-20P) and U3 (ATtiny13V-10S) are present, and each pair of corresponding pins is connected to the same nets, including shared power, reset, and all mapped I/O.",
      "expected": "A controller should use one MCU, or have explicit selection/isolation between alternatives. These two MCUs should not both be populated with their pins hard-paralleled.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"U2\")\n      (value \"ATtiny45-20P\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"U3\")\n      (value \"ATtiny13V-10S\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"6\") (pinfunction \"PB1\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"6\") (pinfunction \"PB1\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "an ATtiny-driven fan controller"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If both processors are assembled, their outputs can contend and the shared reset and programming signals affect both devices. This can cause malfunction or damage and makes programming behavior unreliable.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist ties the I2C SDA/data net directly to the power-input path. It also places two different ATtiny devices on the same power and I/O nets, creating a likely processor-population and output-contention problem."
}

